+/*
+ * Daily Grind client-side performance monitor.
+ *
+ * Measures how long it takes from a user interaction (or a client-side view
+ * switch) until the browser has painted the resulting visual update.
+ *
+ * Tracked interactions:
+ *   - Clicks on the navigation bar            (data-perf-region="nav")
+ *   - Clicks on the hero "Order Now" button   (data-perf-region="order-now")
+ *   - Clicks on "Seasonal Favorites" cards    (data-perf-region="seasonal-card")
+ *   - Client-side view switches (history.pushState, popstate, hashchange, or
+ *     explicit calls to window.dailyGrindPerf.startViewSwitch()).
+ *
+ * Click timing uses the Event Timing API (the same data that powers INP):
+ * an entry's startTime is the event's hardware timestamp and
+ * startTime + duration is the time of the next paint after all handlers ran.
+ * Browsers without Event Timing (or interactions faster than the 16ms
+ * reporting threshold) fall back to a requestAnimationFrame + MessageChannel
+ * "next paint" approximation.
+ *
+ * Results are:
+ *   - recorded as performance.measure() entries ("dg:click:<region>", "dg:view:<name>")
+ *     so they show up in DevTools Performance panel,
+ *   - pushed to window.dailyGrindPerf.metrics,
+ *   - dispatched as a "dailygrind:perf" CustomEvent on window,
+ *   - logged to the console when debugging is enabled (?perfdebug or
+ *     localStorage.dgPerfDebug = "1"),
+ *   - beaconed to the endpoint in <meta name="perf-endpoint" content="..."> (if
+ *     set) when the page is hidden / unloaded.
+ */
