+# The Daily Grind
+
+Static coffee-shop homepage plus a passkey-based **My Account** area (`/account`).
+
+## Running
+
+```sh
+pnpm install
+pnpm start            # node server.js – serves the site and the /api passkey endpoints
+```
+
+| Variable    | Default                    | Purpose                                              |
+|-------------|----------------------------|------------------------------------------------------|
+| `PORT`      | `11222`                    | HTTP port                                            |
+| `RP_ID`     | `localhost`                | WebAuthn Relying Party ID – your site's domain       |
+| `RP_NAME`   | `The Daily Grind`          | Name shown in passkey prompts                        |
+| `ORIGINS`   | `http://localhost:$PORT`   | Comma-separated origins allowed to use passkeys      |
+| `DATA_FILE` | `./data/db.json`           | JSON file where users and passkey public keys are kept |
+
+Passkeys only work on `https://` origins or `localhost`. In production set e.g.
+`RP_ID=dailygrind.example ORIGINS=https://dailygrind.example` (cookies then become `Secure`/`__Host-`).
+
+## Account features
+
+- **Create account** – name + email, then a discoverable passkey is created (user verification required).
+- **Sign in** – passkey autofill in the email field (conditional mediation) or a "Sign in with a passkey" button.
+- **Passkeys** – list with provider name (from AAGUID), synced/device-bound status, created & last-used dates;
+  rename, remove (never the last one), and create additional passkeys.
+- **Profile** – change name or email.
+- **Reauthentication** – changing email, adding/removing passkeys and deleting the account need a passkey check
+  from the last 5 minutes; the UI prompts for it automatically and retries.
+- **Signal API** – keeps passkey providers in sync (`signalUnknownCredential`, `signalAllAcceptedCredentials`,
+  `signalCurrentUserDetails`) where the browser supports it.
+
+## Notes
+
+- Sessions are kept in memory (signing in again is needed after a restart); challenges are single use and expire
+  after 5 minutes. State-changing API calls require a matching `Origin` header (CSRF protection).
+- The JSON file store is meant for demos/small deployments; swap `loadDb`/`saveDb` in `server.js` for a real database.
