 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Passkeys
+
+Sign-in (`/signin`), sign-up (`/signup`) and account settings (`/account`) support passkeys:
+
+- **Sign in** with passkey autofill on the username field (`autocomplete="username webauthn"`) or the "Sign in with a passkey" button. After a password sign-in, the browser may silently offer to save a passkey (conditional create).
+- **Sign up** offers to create a passkey right after the account is created.
+- **Account settings** lists passkeys (provider icon/name, created and last-used dates), and lets users create, rename and delete them. The list is kept in sync with password managers via the WebAuthn Signal API.
+- **Reauthentication**: deleting a passkey or changing the display name requires a sign-in or verification (passkey, or password fallback) within the last 5 minutes.
+
+Server endpoints live in `src/pages/api/auth/` and use [SimpleWebAuthn](https://simplewebauthn.dev/) for verification. Configuration (environment variables):
+
+| Variable | Default | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `RP_ID` | request hostname | WebAuthn Relying Party ID (e.g. a registrable parent domain) |
+| `WEBAUTHN_ORIGINS` | request origin (+ its `https://` form) | Comma-separated allowed origins |
+| `AUTH_DB_PATH` | `$TMPDIR/devtools-times-auth.json` | JSON file storing local users and passkeys — point this at persistent storage in production |
+
+Password accounts remain in the Times API; the app proxies password sign-in/sign-up through `/api/auth/login` and `/api/auth/register` to establish a server session.
