+
+## Passkeys
+
+Sign-in, sign-up and account settings support passkeys (WebAuthn) via [SimpleWebAuthn](https://simplewebauthn.dev/):
+
+- **Sign up** (`/signup`): after creating an account with a password, users are signed in and offered to create a passkey.
+- **Sign in** (`/signin`): "Sign in with a passkey" button plus passkey autofill (conditional UI) on the username field. After a password sign-in, accounts without a passkey get an automatic passkey upgrade (where the browser supports conditional create) or an explicit offer.
+- **Account settings** (`/account`): list, create, rename and remove passkeys. Adding or removing a passkey requires a sign-in within the last 5 minutes; otherwise the user is asked to confirm it's them with a passkey or their password.
+- The WebAuthn Signal API keeps password managers in sync when passkeys are removed or unknown.
+
+Passwords are still verified by the upstream account API (proxied through `/api/auth/*`). Passkeys and user handles are stored in `.data/passkeys.json` (override with `PASSKEY_STORE_PATH`). The relying party ID and origin default to the request's host; pin them with `PASSKEY_RP_ID` and `PASSKEY_ORIGINS` (comma-separated) if needed.
