+# Privacy by Design — The Daily Grind website
+
+This is the engineering checklist that keeps the public site privacy-preserving by default.
+Update it whenever a dependency, form, or header changes.
+
+## 1. Data minimization
+
+- The homepage collects **no** personal data: no forms other than logout, no cookies set
+  client-side, and nothing written to `localStorage` / `sessionStorage`.
+- Sessions must use a server-set cookie:
+  `Set-Cookie: __Host-session=…; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax; Path=/`.
+- Future forms (ordering, rewards sign-up) must:
+  - ask only for fields needed for that task (e.g. birthday *month* for a rewards treat,
+    not full date of birth; phone number optional);
+  - explain inline, next to the field, why each field is requested;
+  - offer guest checkout for online orders;
+  - use data only for the purpose stated at collection.
+- Server logs must mask emails, tokens and IDs. CSP violation reports (`/reports/csp`)
+  must have query strings stripped before storage.
+
+## 2. Third-party inventory & audit
+
+| Origin | Purpose | Data exposed | Status |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| *(none)* | — | — | All assets (CSS, JS, images) are self-hosted |
+
+Previously the hero image was hot-linked from `images.unsplash.com`, which exposed every
+visitor's IP address, User-Agent and page URL (via `Referer`) to a third party. It is now
+served from `/images/` (Unsplash License, photo `photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085`; checked
+for EXIF/GPS metadata, none present).
+
+Before adding any third party:
+
+1. Justify the need; prefer a self-hosted or static-HTML alternative (e.g. plain share
+   links instead of social SDKs, a click-to-load façade instead of a map/video embed).
+2. Pin to an immutable versioned URL and add `integrity="sha384-…" crossorigin="anonymous"
+   referrerpolicy="no-referrer"`.
+3. Add its origin to the narrowest CSP directive in **both** `_headers` and the `<meta>`
+   CSP in `index.html`, and relax `Permissions-Policy` only for features it truly needs.
+4. Add a row to the table above and update the public privacy policy.
+5. Never load third parties on account, rewards, or checkout pages.
+
+Audit quarterly (and on every release that touches markup): record a HAR in DevTools with
+cache disabled, confirm every request is same-origin, and review the DevTools Issues panel
+and `/reports/csp` for violations.
+
+## 3. Headers (see `_headers`)
+
+- **CSP**: `default-src 'none'` with only first-party sources, no inline script/style,
+  `frame-ancestors 'none'`, Trusted Types enforced, reporting to a first-party endpoint.
+- **Referrer-Policy: same-origin**: no URL information leaks to other sites.
+- **Permissions-Policy**: camera, microphone, geolocation, sensors, and ad/tracking APIs
+  (Topics, Protected Audience, Attribution Reporting) disabled.
+- **Clear-Site-Data** on `/logout`; `Cache-Control: no-store` on personal pages.
+- HSTS, `X-Content-Type-Options`, `X-Frame-Options`, COOP, CORP.
+
+## 4. User control
+
+- `/.well-known/gpc.json` declares that the site honors Global Privacy Control. Because
+  there is no sale/sharing of data and no trackers, GPC requires no behavior change today;
+  any future integration must check `Sec-GPC: 1` / `navigator.globalPrivacyControl` and
+  treat it as an opt-out.
+- `/account/privacy` ("Your Data") must let signed-in users download, correct, and delete
+  their data without contacting support.
+- Logout is a `POST` form; `js/privacy.js` additionally clears Web Storage, Cache Storage
+  and service workers as a fallback for browsers without full `Clear-Site-Data` support.
