@@ -0,0 +1,121 @@
+# Privacy by Design: The Daily Grind website
+
+This document records the privacy decisions behind the site's markup, scripts,
+and HTTP headers. Update it whenever something that touches personal data or a
+third party changes.
+
+Last reviewed: 2026-11-20
+
+## 1. Principles
+
+| Principle | How it's applied |
+|---|---|
+| Proactive, not reactive | Strict CSP and Permissions-Policy block capabilities and third parties we don't use, so they can't be added by accident. |
+| Privacy as the default | Every non-essential consent category starts **off**. Nothing is written to storage until the visitor makes a choice. No consent banner, because there's nothing to opt out of. |
+| Embedded into design | Privacy controls live in `assets/js/privacy.js` and `_headers`, not in a third-party consent platform. |
+| Full functionality | The site works fully with JS disabled and with every optional category off. |
+| End-to-end security | HSTS, an HTTPS upgrade, logout over POST, Clear-Site-Data on logout, and no-store caching for personalized pages. |
+| Visibility and transparency | This file, the "Privacy Choices" dialog, the footer notice, and `/.well-known/gpc.json`. |
+| Respect for the user | Global Privacy Control and Do Not Track are treated as a binding opt-out that the UI can't override. |
+
+## 2. Data inventory (client side)
+
+| Data | Where | Purpose | Contents | Retention | Category |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `dg_privacy_consent` | `localStorage` | Remember the visitor's privacy choice | Policy version, date (YYYY-MM-DD, no time of day), three booleans | 365 days or until the policy version changes, then deleted automatically | Strictly necessary |
+| Session cookie (server) | Cookie | Sign-in | Opaque ID. Must be `HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax` (or `Strict`) with the `__Host-` prefix | Session or a short idle timeout | Strictly necessary |
+
+Nothing else is collected on the client. No fingerprinting, no analytics, no
+advertising IDs, and no IP-based location lookups.
+
+**Data minimization in practice**
+
+- The consent record is rebuilt from a fixed schema on every read, so unknown
+  fields are thrown away.
+- Marketing and analytics tracking parameters (`utm_*`, `gclid`, `fbclid`,
+  `msclkid`, and so on) are removed from the address bar on load. They aren't
+  kept in history, and they aren't passed along when visitors share links.
+- `format-detection` stops mobile browsers from turning text into tappable
+  phone, email, or address links.
+- The hero image is self-hosted, with its metadata (including the ICC profile)
+  removed using `convert -strip`.
+- `robots.txt` and `X-Robots-Tag` keep account and order pages out of search
+  indexes.
+
+## 3. Third-party audit
+
+| Third party | Previously used for | Data exposed | Decision |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `images.unsplash.com` (Unsplash CDN) | Hero background image | Visitor IP, User-Agent, Referer (page URL), and request timing on every page view | **Removed.** The image (Unsplash License) is now self-hosted at `assets/img/hero.jpg`. |
+
+**Current third parties: none.** The CSP (`default-src 'none'` plus `'self'`
+only) enforces this in the browser.
+
+**Adding a third party requires all of the following:**
+
+1. A written review appended to the table above covering what data it receives,
+   whether it sets cookies or identifiers, where it processes data, whether a
+   DPA is in place, and its retention period.
+2. A consent category, if the service isn't strictly necessary.
+3. An entry in `THIRD_PARTY_REGISTRY` in `assets/js/privacy.js`.
+4. Loading through a consent-gated placeholder rather than a plain `<script>`:
+   ```html
+   <script type="text/plain" data-consent="analytics"
+           data-src="https://vendor.example/script.js"
+           data-integrity="sha384-..."></script>
+   ```
+   `privacy.js` only activates it after consent, only if it's in the registry,
+   and only if it has a Subresource Integrity hash. It's loaded with
+   `referrerpolicy="no-referrer"`.
+5. Adding the specific origin (never a wildcard) to the CSP in **both**
+   `_headers` and the `<meta>` tag in `index.html`.
+6. GPC and DNT will still block `analytics` and `marketing` services.
+
+## 4. Security headers (`_headers`)
+
+| Header | Value / purpose |
+|---|---|
+| `Content-Security-Policy` | `default-src 'none'`, with only same-origin scripts, styles, and images allowed. No `unsafe-inline` and no `unsafe-eval`. Also sets `frame-ancestors 'none'`, `form-action 'self'`, `base-uri 'none'`, and `upgrade-insecure-requests`. The `<meta>` copy in `index.html` is a fallback, because statikk (the local static server) can't set headers. |
+| `Strict-Transport-Security` | 2 years, includeSubDomains, preload |
+| `Referrer-Policy` | `strict-origin-when-cross-origin`: full URLs (which may contain order or account paths) never leave the site |
+| `Permissions-Policy` | Turns off camera, microphone, geolocation, payment, sensors, FLoC/Topics, and more |
+| `Cross-Origin-*-Policy` | Isolates the browsing context from cross-origin windows and embeds |
+| `X-Content-Type-Options`, `X-Frame-Options` | Prevent MIME sniffing and clickjacking |
+| `X-DNS-Prefetch-Control: off` | No speculative DNS lookups that leak which links are on the page |
+| `Cache-Control: no-store` | On pages that may show personal data (`/`, `/account`, `/rewards`, `/order-online`, `/logout`) |
+| `Clear-Site-Data` | On `/logout`: clears cache, cookies, and storage |
+
+`_headers` uses the Netlify / Cloudflare Pages format. On nginx, Apache, or a
+CDN, copy the same values into that server's config.
+
+## 5. Secure data handling
+
+- **Logout** is a `POST` form, not a GET link. That way it can't be triggered
+  by a cross-site `<img>`, by link prefetching, or by crawlers.
+  `privacy.js` first clears `sessionStorage`, non-essential `localStorage`,
+  JS-visible cookies, and Cache Storage. The server response should include
+  `Clear-Site-Data` and expire the session cookie server-side.
+- **Withdrawing consent** for Preferences immediately deletes the
+  non-essential `localStorage` data.
+- **Expiring consent:** choices expire after 12 months or when
+  `POLICY_VERSION` changes. Expired records are deleted, not just ignored.
+- **Failing closed:** if storage is blocked, there's a parse error, or a
+  category is unknown, the result is "no consent".
+
+## 6. Server-side requirements (out of scope for this static repo)
+
+- Session cookie: `__Host-session=...; Path=/; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax`.
+- CSRF token on `POST /logout` and on all state-changing forms.
+- Read the `Sec-GPC: 1` request header and treat it as an opt-out of
+  sale/sharing (CCPA/CPRA, Colorado, and similar).
+- Don't log full IP addresses or query strings. Truncate or anonymize logs and
+  keep them for 30 days or less.
+
+## 7. Review checklist (run before each release)
+
+- [ ] `grep -rn "https://" index.html assets/` shows no third-party resource URLs
+- [ ] No inline `<script>`, inline `style=""`, or inline event handlers (required by the CSP)
+- [ ] The CSP is identical in `_headers` and `index.html` (except for `frame-ancestors` and `upgrade-insecure-requests`, which can't go in the meta tag)
+- [ ] New storage keys or cookies are added to the data inventory
+- [ ] New third parties have a completed audit entry
+- [ ] `POLICY_VERSION` is bumped if categories or purposes changed
